# Git Commit Rules

- Messages in English, Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <description>`
- Imperative subject (`add`, `fix`, `remove`); one logical change per commit
- No commit body unless needed for constraints/tradeoffs/multi-subsystem context
- Do not push without explicit user approval
- Never commit secrets, debug junk, unrelated files, or local artifacts

## Types

`feat` | `fix` | `refactor` | `test` | `docs` | `chore`

## Scopes (preferred)

`api` | `web` | `auth` | `db` | `shared` | `books` | `reader` | `admin` | `rules` | `infra`

## Examples

```text
fix(api): add missing book chat prompt template
feat(web): add chapter vocabulary panel
docs(rules): migrate agent rules to Cursor
```

## Before commit

Run the smallest relevant verification (targeted test, lint, or typecheck). Review the staged diff so every file belongs to the same logical change.
